{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you, encamp outside the camp.</b> Even though one impure from a corpse is permitted even in the camp of Leviyyah, they did not want them to enter it — we are concerned lest they render others impure, for they were many and could not be careful of them, and also they were fathers of impurity to render persons and vessels impure." "<b>You shall purify yourselves.</b> Rashi explained: with the waters of the נדה, like the law of other corpse-impurities, etc. — until he concedes that Canaanites defile through contact. And if you ask: but regarding one who touches as well, אדם is written, as it is written: ״וכל אשר יגע על פני השדה בחלל חרב או במת או בעצם אדם״ — if so, we should exclude Canaanites from defiling through touching, for you are called אדם, as it is written in Ezekiel: ״ואתן צאני צאן מרעיתי אדם אתם״ — and not the Canaanites. Rather, one may answer: since the verse went back and repeated regarding touching, in the matter of sprinkling, without אדם, as it is written: ״והזה על האהל ועל הנוגע בעצם או בחלל או במת או בקבר״ — we include, that even a Canaanite defiles through touching." "<b>On the third day and on the seventh day.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, required sprinkling of third and seventh for the war against Midian — which was not done so in the war against the seven nations. For in the war against the seven nations, all Israel were present and impurity was permitted in a public congregation, and even the stews of Canaanites were not forbidden to them, for even walls of swine were permitted, as it is written: ״ובתים מלאים כל טוב״ — even walls of swine. But here, against Midian, who are not among the seven nations, and none of Israel were there except a thousand per tribe, the stews of Canaanites were forbidden to them, and also they required sprinkling of third and seventh, because they became impure through contact when they killed the Midianites. And further, because some of Israel became impure through them, as it is written: ״ויצמד ישראל לבעל פעור״. And further, perhaps one Israelite was killed of the twelve thousand, and what is written, ״ולא נפקד ממנו איש״ — that is for the matter of sin; and out of doubt regarding impurity as well they required sprinkling."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:26.865533019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}